# screens/

One folder per screen. Every screen folder uses the **strict 4-subfolder
rule** — no files live at the screen root.

## The strict 4-subfolder rule

| Subfolder | What lives here | Naming suffix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/` | Screen-local presentational components | `*.tsx` |
| `hooks/` | Screen-local hooks (`useThing.ts`) | `use*.ts` |
| `services/` | Business logic / API orchestration | `*.service.ts` |
| `types/` | Types and interfaces local to the screen | `*.types.ts` |

The screen component itself (e.g. `HomeScreen.tsx`) is the only `.tsx` at
the screen root — it composes pieces from the four subfolders into the
final UI. The screen file is the navigator-registered component.

